        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(skills): normalize ClawHub search limits and cleanup legacy constants",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAdds defensive test coverage for ClawHub skill and package search limit forwarding behavior. Ensures that configured limits are passed through verbatim to the ClawHub API, or omitted entirely when absent.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Added transport-layer tests for `searchClawHubSkills` and `searchClawHubPackages` limit forwarding\n- Added lifecycle-layer tests for `searchClawHubSkills` limit handling\n- Removed unsupported `999_999` package-limit assertion per ClawSweeper P2 finding\n- Tests verify:\n  - Valid limits forwarded unchanged\n  - Fractional limits preserved\n  - Omitted limits not added to URL\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Environment**: macOS Vitest (Node 22.22.2)\n\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch**:\n```bash\nnpx vitest run src/infra/clawhub.test.ts src/skills/lifecycle/clawhub.test.ts\n```\n\n**Observed result after fix**:\n```text\n✓ infra src/infra/clawhub.test.ts (75 tests) 358ms\n✓ skills-lifecycle src/skills/lifecycle/clawhub.test.ts (79 tests) 412ms\n\nTest Files  2 passed (2)\nTests  154 passed (154)\n```\n\n**Key test coverage**:\n- `searchClawHubSkills` limit forwarding: valid, fractional, omitted\n- `searchClawHubPackages` limit forwarding: valid (5), omitted\n- Removed: oversized `999_999` assertion (unsupported per ClawHub 1-100 contract)\n\n**What was not tested**: Live ClawHub API requests (mocked fetch implementation)\n\n## Regression Test Plan\n- Coverage: 154 tests across 2 files\n- Target files: `src/infra/clawhub.test.ts`, `src/skills/lifecycle/clawhub.test.ts`\n- Scenarios locked in:\n  - Valid limit forwarded verbatim\n  - Fractional limit preserved\n  - Omitted limit excluded from URL\n",
